  "english": "23. Thursday. [Tone 3, or implied]: Vahan of Goghtn, and\nEugenia the Virgin, and the others.\n25. Saturday. Of the Patriarchs Athanasius and\nCyril.\n26. Sunday. Second [Sunday]. Barekendan [Pre-Lenten Fast Eve] of the Fast of the Catechumens. See according to the order, and the rest.\n[Section Break / Note]\n14. Friday. Presentation of the Lord [Tyarnndaraj].\n16. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Great Barekendan [Eve of Great Lent]. See\nthe First Volume from this point until Vardavar, keeping the local order.\n\n6. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADz]. Easter [Zatik]. Day of the Resurrection\nof Christ.\n7. Monday. Tone 2 [AK]. Second day of Easter, and\nFeast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin.\nMay\n15. Thursday. Tone 8 [DK]. Ascension of Christ.\n25. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK]. Pentecost (Coming of the Holy Spirit).\nBarekendan of the Fast of Elijah.\nJune\n1. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADz]. First [Sunday]. Beginning of the Resurrection\nSundays. Canticle [Harts] [Tone 3, ADz]: \"Who didst come\" (Vor ekir). See according to the order in the First\nVolume.\nJuly\n13. Sunday. Tone 3 [BDz]. Vardavar [Transfiguration]. The period of eating meat [non-fasting period]\nis four weeks. Until the Friday of the third\nweek, see the First\nVolume, and on Saturday come here and\ncelebrate the feasts written below, which\nbelong to the Octave of the Nativity.\nAugust\n2. Saturday. Tone 7 [DDz]. Gregory the Theologian.\n3. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Fourth [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 4 [BK]: \"Who [wast sent] from the heavenly hosts\" (Vor yerknayin zin). Responsorial [Hambartsi] Tone 8 [DK]: \"When they came\" (Yorzham yekin), and \"The Angel descended\" (Yej hreshtakn).\n4. Monday. Tone 1 [ADz]. Eugenius, Macarius,\nand the others. Canticle [Harts] Tone 7 [DDz]: \"Holy art Thou, Lord of\nHosts\" (Surb es ter zorutyants).\n5. Tuesday. Tone 2 [AK]. Andrew the General, and\nhis army, and the others.\n7. Thursday. Tone 4 [BK]. Adrian and his wife, and the others.\nCanticle [Harts] Tone 8 [DK]: \"To Thee, O God\" (Ar kez astvats).\n9. Saturday. Tone 8 [DK]. The Holy Council of Ephesus\nof the two hundred Patriarchs.\n10. Sunday. Tone 7 [DDz]. Fifth [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 5 [GDz]:\n\"We glorify Thee\" (Paravoremk zkez). Responsorial [Hambartsi] Tone 7 [DDz]:\n\"Of the Women\" (Kanantsn). Barekendan [Eve] of the Fast of the Holy\nMother of God.\n11. Monday. Tone 8 [DK]. Fast of the Holy Mother of God.\nPenitential Canticle [Harts Alts] Tone 3 [BDz]: \"Who didst save\" (Vor apretsuter).\n17. Sunday. Tone 6 [GK]. Assumption of the Holy\nMother of God. The period of eating meat [non-fasting period] is three\nweeks. See the First Volume\nuntil the fourth Sunday, keeping\nthe local order.\nSeptember\n7. Sunday. Tone 3 [BDz]. Fourth [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 6 [GK]: \"Ineffable\" (Anjeli). Responsorial [Hambartsi] Tone 3 [BDz]: \"At the tomb\" (I gerezman),\nand \"They came to the tomb\" (Yekin i gerez). Barekendan\nof the Holy Cross.\n8. Monday. Tone 4 [BK]. Fast of the Holy Cross. - Feast of the\nNativity of the Holy Mother of God.\n9. Tuesday. Tone 5 [GDz]. Of the Fast. Penitential Canticle [Harts Alts] Tone 4 [BK]:\n\"Lord God\" (Ter astvats).\n14. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK]. Exaltation of the Holy Cross [Khachverats]. See the First\nVolume until the tenth Sunday.\nBut for the Canticles of the Martyrs and the Fast,\nand the Resurrection Responsorials [Hambartsis], and the Tone of the\ndays, look in the Calendar of Letters [K Taregirk],\nkeeping the month.\nNovember\n16. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADz]. Tenth [Sunday]. Responsorial [Hambartsi] Tone 1 [ADz]:\n\"Who ineffable\" (Vor anchar), to the end. Barekendan [Eve]\nof the Fast of the Advent [Hisnak].\n17. Monday. Tone 2 [AK]. Fast of the Advent. Canticle [Harts]\nTone 7 [DDz]: \"Of our fathers, God, who in\ntribulation\" (Hartsən merots astvats vor i neghutian).\n21. Friday. Tone 6 [GK]. Feast of the Presentation of the Holy\nMother of God.",
